    "title": "The Pocket Museum",
    "passage": "Sam was helping Zoe sort clothes before putting them away. In one coat pocket, he found a small stone and a paper ticket. Zoe remembered collecting the stone on a walk with their grandfather. The ticket was from a train journey they had taken the same day. Sam put both things on the table and asked what was in the next pocket. They found a button, a little drawing, and a folded shopping list. Zoe could remember a story for almost every object. Sam arranged them in a row and made paper labels for them. He called their table a museum of ordinary days. Zoe put the shopping list back because they still needed it. Then she added a label to the empty place where it had been. It said that this part of the museum had gone shopping.",
